lowers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-30T01:57:11Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T02:00:36Z","body":"Regression from #121879 as this PR add a call to `_update_bvh` (where the crash happens) when `EditorNode3DGizmo.set_hidden()` is called. But even before #121879 you could crash the editor by trying to drag and select the node with the gizmo using the same MRP:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9e7a34a6-2a37-44c3-8389-dd5d797d9c6d\n\n<br>\n<br>\n\nAnd even with the proposed changes (which fixes both the original crash and the one i mentined above), the editor throw errors complaining about the null `gizmo_plugin` by select and unselect the node, which makes me wonder if the root problem is allow the `EditorNode3DGizmo` without a gizmo plugin attached.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4cb992f5-02ed-4253-961b-f86c0a5aa935","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5902553180/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]